---
import { portfolio } from '../lib/content';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import EvidenceLinks from '../components/EvidenceLinks.astro';
import PersonaControl from '../components/PersonaControl.astro';
---
<Layout title="Architecture" description="Source-described project architectures and an honest account of this static portfolio’s implemented and planned capabilities.">
  <div class="reading"><header class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">System notes / not a simulation</p><h1>How the pieces<br />fit together.</h1><p>Two source-described project flows. One transparent account of this portfolio’s own runtime.</p></header>
    <nav class="reading-nav" aria-label="Architecture sections"><a href="#project-architectures">Project architectures</a><a href="#runtime">This website</a><a href="#job-description">JD workspace</a><a href="#observatory">Observatory</a></nav>
    <PersonaControl />
    <section id="project-architectures"><h2>What the public sources establish</h2><p>These records describe systems. They do not invent technology-selection rationale or attribute unreported decisions.</p>
      {portfolio.decisions.map((decision, index) => <article class="record" id={decision.id}><h3>{decision.title}</h3><p>{decision.summary}</p>
        <ol class="flow" aria-label={index === 0 ? 'Source-described telemetry sequence' : 'Source-described governance sequence'}>{(index === 0 ? ['OpenTelemetry', 'Postgres', 'Azure Data Explorer', 'Elasticsearch', 'Next.js'] : ['Policy & findings', 'Remediation plan', 'Human approval', 'Execution & post-state', 'Evidence pack']).map((step) => <li>{step}</li>)}</ol>
        <EvidenceLinks ids={decision.evidenceIds} />
      </article>)}
      <p class="note">Forecasting project perspectives explicitly identify unanswered engineering questions. They are not claims of implemented validation, retraining, or uncertainty-handling strategies.</p>
    </section>
    <section id="runtime"><p class="eyebrow">Behind this atlas</p><h2>Static first. Enhancements second.</h2>
      <ol class="flow" aria-label="Portfolio build sequence">{['Canonical public JSON', 'Zod validation', 'Build Brain indexes', 'Astro static HTML', 'Optional browser controls'].map((step) => <li>{step}</li>)}</ol>
      <div class="runtime-grid">
        <article class="runtime-card"><p class="status-tag">IMPLEMENTED / STATIC</p><h3>The complete portfolio</h3><p>Pre-rendered project dossiers, experience, education, credentials, evidence, skills, journeys, contact, and résumé. Real links work without JavaScript. Structured domain lanes are editorial groupings.</p></article>
        <article class="runtime-card" id="build-brain"><p class="status-tag">IMPLEMENTED / BUILD TIME</p><h3>Build Brain</h3><p>Validated JSON produces hash-versioned indexes and a Markdown résumé. Pinned MiniLM q8 inference creates real 384-dimensional normalized embeddings for the 37 canonical excerpts. The browser uses the same model revision, tokenizer, dtype and pooling.</p></article>
        <article class="runtime-card" id="pocket-runtime"><p class="status-tag">IMPLEMENTED / LOCAL WORKER</p><h3>Pocket, with or without a model</h3><p>Bounded lexical/concept retrieval and conservative JD matching need no model. Optional learned semantic retrieval runs single-threaded WASM inside the Pocket worker. Deterministic tools only accept known IDs and sections.</p></article>
        <article class="runtime-card" id="full-runtime"><p class="status-tag">OPTIONAL / CAPABILITY-GATED</p><h3>Full evidence selection</h3><p>Qwen runs in a separate WebGPU worker after consent. It produces constrained JSON evidence IDs, never displayed prose. IDs must belong to Pocket’s retrieved set. Suggested actions require confirmation; failure returns to Pocket, then deterministic retrieval, then the static catalog.</p></article>
      </div>
      <article class="record" id="distribution"><h3>Static distribution, not a live backend</h3><p>GitHub Pages is the intended static host. Local validation and Pages release workflows are implemented; they publish only audited static output after checks pass. They have not been executed on GitHub by this task, and this page does not assert a live deployment.</p></article>
      <article class="record" id="dns-resolution"><h3>Domain resolution</h3><ol class="flow" aria-label="Intended static delivery path"><li>kevilpatel.in</li><li>GoDaddy DNS</li><li>GitHub Pages</li><li>Static HTML</li><li>Optional local workers</li></ol><p class="note">Intended topology, not a network probe or a claim that DNS was changed.</p></article>
      <details><summary>Privacy, storage, and failure behavior</summary><div class="disclosure-body"><p>Enhanced search and JD text remain in browser memory. No query telemetry or backend is used. Appearance uses local storage; the reading lens uses session storage. Native no-JS GET search puts its query in the URL and sends it to the static host; do not enter sensitive text there.</p><p>A service worker installs a hash-verified snapshot of public pages, small interface assets, knowledge indexes and the model-free Pocket worker. No model SDK, weights or WASM are precached. Updates wait for explicit refresh; offline-page clearing does not clear models. Recent history contains at most eight public route paths, never query strings. External links still need a network. Full offline inference remains unproven. <a href="/offline/">Offline limitations and recovery</a>.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>Evidence and comparison rules</summary><div class="disclosure-body"><p>Every comparison uses the same canonical summaries, technologies, perspectives, and excerpts. No fit score, winner, personal tradeoff, or proficiency level is inferred. Source-listed credentials retain their verification limitations.</p></div></details>
    </section>
    <section id="job-description"><p class="status-tag">LOCAL / EVIDENCE ONLY</p><h2>Job-description workspace</h2><p>Compare individual requirements to exact public evidence. Strong Evidence requires an explicit project/skill join. Skill-only or semantic matches are Related, not proof of proficiency. Unknown or negated requirements are Not Demonstrated. No percentage score.</p>
      <form data-jd-form autocomplete="off"><label class="label" for="local-jd">Paste requirements · maximum 12,000 characters</label><textarea id="local-jd" data-jd-input maxlength="12000" rows="7" disabled spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="jd-privacy" placeholder="Python; LangGraph; Java; Rust; 5 years of AWS"></textarea><p class="note" id="jd-privacy">Ephemeral browser memory only. Never uploaded, saved, placed in the URL, or sent to a model host. No file upload. Clear removes the pasted text and results.</p><div class="actions"><button type="submit" class="primary" data-jd-submit disabled>Review local evidence</button><button type="button" data-jd-clear>Clear pasted text</button></div></form>
      <p data-jd-status role="status" aria-live="polite">JavaScript enables local analysis. Without it, browse the source-linked skills below.</p><div data-jd-results></div>
      <a class="text-link" href="/evidence/#skills">Browse source-linked skills →</a>
    </section>
    <section id="observatory"><p class="eyebrow">Observed state / not simulated metrics</p><h2>Runtime observatory</h2><p>Selected and loaded models are separate. No adapter identifiers are collected. GPU/storage probing is on demand; unknown is not zero. Durations are measured for this page’s operations, not promised performance.</p><button type="button" data-observatory-refresh>Measure capabilities and caches</button><pre class="observatory" data-observatory>JavaScript is disabled: static portfolio only. No model loaded.</pre><ol class="flow" aria-label="Local trust and fallback boundaries"><li>Question / JD in memory</li><li>Pocket worker</li><li>Optional Full ID selection</li><li>Schema + evidence allowlist</li><li>Canonical excerpts / confirmed tools</li><li>Deterministic → static fallback</li></ol></section>
    <section aria-labelledby="offline-observed"><h2 id="offline-observed">Offline observatory</h2><p>Actual registration, waiting update, cache entry counts and bounded public route history. A complete count is not proof against later eviction or corruption; cached responses are hash-checked when read. Network availability is only a browser hint.</p><pre class="observatory" data-offline-observatory>Not measured. JavaScript and a secure context are required for offline installation.</pre></section>
  </div>
</Layout>